      "title": "Informal Trade Behind Wiregrass Restoration",
      "blurb": "Interviews with 20 Florida landowners, land managers, and conservation staff show wiregrass restoration runs on trust-based swaps of seed, burn crews, and equipment. Seed costs about $1,700 per pound, and goodwill, more than profit, drives the sharing.",
